<<~ ahu slot=`#/node-control-home-before-any-face-not-built-exac`>>

!! (2) Node control home before any face — NOT BUILT; exact map
The reorder is mechanically small (init.ts runInit: after `foundThePlace` (~l.425) call `standVesselSecretHome(repo)` then `nameControlHome(place.daemonHandle, secret.controlUrl)`, mirroring browser open-browser-vessel.ts ~l.972; `runFoundTheFace` l.657 then opens the standing home and the daemon's first name holds; fleet-join land l.319 opens it too). It is blocked by a RULING COLLISION, not code:
* Operator ruling 2026-11-09, in code and canon: "THE PLACE MINTS NO SECRET HOME AND NO CONTROL DOCUMENT … both mint with the FACE … a herm that never lights a face holds neither" (init.ts l.421-424; floor-verbs.ts header; control-home.ts standControlHome doc).
* On the node a herm is NOT a founding class: `runInit` founds one place; "herm" is a stand-time choice (`--recipe herm` → `askedStanding`, main.ts l.126) or the forced standing of any faceless/locked place (`standAs`, main.ts l.407). So "control home at place founding" makes EVERY node place, herm included, name one, against "a herm names none".
* The fork to rule: (a) founding grows a class bit (`lares vessel found --herm` founds no control home; the default founds the veil floor's), or (b) the control home mints at the first unlock of a non-herm standing (composeHearthStanding over an open key and no face), or (c) the herm keeps a named home its composition never stands.
* Tests that encode the 2026-11-09 ruling and must move by intent once ruled: secret-home-placement "RED (Gaia Thursday): a place founding (a herm, no face) mints no secret home and no control document"; uds-floor-answers F1/F2/F4 (Saltmere herm); direct-holder-refused-unlock U2; device-admit-face-edge; cabal-join; tools/mesh-scenarios-probe.test.mjs; tools/floor-unlock-door F1 (fresh boot then reads `vessel-locked` stand-in, not unnamed).
* Runtime to verify after: open-node-vessel's faceless path ("working layer held in memory at the floor (control-home-unnamed)") should stand the floor working slot through keyhive `floorWorking` once control reads (shared code, browser-proven); the floor verb gate (keyhive veil-floor-verbs G1) then lets the unlocked veil mint.
* (3) W4: drop `NODE_VEIL_STANDS`, and ask through a served front (start `serveUdsFront`/`makeUdsSeat` in the vector, or call the daemon's `placeVerb` and read the outcome from the control store), not `storeClaim.socketPath`.

