<<~ ahu slot=`#/finding-resend-exhaustion-under-a-slow-rest`>>

!! FINDING (fork for the controller): resend exhaustion under a slow rest
projection-sink resends every pending act at each fresh frame and each new relay (777ea3764, bound 3). vessel-host refuses a resend while the first still waits (55b631484, `control-event-pending`), and that refused resend still counts. An act's result waits on `receipt.held()` (every hold in flight), so under quick successive acts a close-click's answer arrives after 3 frames: the page ends it `binding-unavailable`, then the late `applied` arrives to nothing. Faced and veil alike. CI golden W6's plate (`binding-unavailable`) reads as this. Cure shapes (untried): (a) the vessel tells the page a resend met a pending act, and the page counts no attempt for it; (b) the page resends only at a re-arm (doors replaced), where an answer can actually be lost. Both move a deliberate law in vessel-host/projection-sink.

<<~/ahu>>

