<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-open-defect`>>

!! THE OPEN DEFECT (first thing for a successor)
A veil floor refuses the receipt of an act made through the PROJECTION (the island's own editor, drafts included).
* Repro, no e2e: vite on a scratch LAR_ROOT, then `node /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/veil/smoke/smoke6.mjs <out> http://localhost:5173/ 3`. It prints `REFUSAL at 1 receipt-refused@3`, the page logs `[vessel] a control event refused: control-event-pending …` on each resend, and three unanswered sends end as `binding-unavailable` (golden W6's plate; golden W1 on the first run was the same act never answered).
* The mirror path stays whole (smoke2: write, rest 21/21/0, reload, read back).
* Diagnosis, read off the code and NOT yet confirmed by naming the document: `receiptInStore` refuses when the vessel's copy never comes to hold the island's heads. A veil's DRAFT and PERSONAL slot documents stand as `vessel-only` binding documents (daemon-bag bindings, catalog floor drafts), and the share verdict keeps a vessel-only document from every wiki island unless `deviceDocs.floorWiki(documentId)` (browser `browserShareConfig`, node `vesselOnlyShareVerdict`). Only the floor's `working` and `canon` slots file there. So the wiki island's draft and personal documents never reach the vessel, and each act that touches one refuses its receipt.
* The cure's shape: file the veil floor's draft and personal slots as the vessel's own, as `working` files (`slot-doc-resolver.ts` `floorWorking`: mint the id ahead, `announceFloor(slug, kind, id)`, control row `floor-slot/<slug>/<kind>`, THEN the first byte). NAMED BEFORE THE FIRST BYTE matters: a held bag refuses a clear chunk at rest (`held-clear-at-rest`), so naming an already-rested document would break its load. Then widen `announceFloor`'s kind in slot-doc-resolver.ts and its one wiring line in operator-daemon-behavior.ts (~line 490, away from Leaf-Wright's two sites), and have the Lift drop the two control rows when their bindings lift (anon-lift steps 2-3). Reds: a veil's projection act answers `applied`; the floor draft rests under the vessel's seal mark.
* canon the-veil-ladder says "a draft and a personal margin rest beside it the same way"; the seal filing for those two never landed. True that line or build it.

<<~/ahu>>

